2etd|n|The act of vibrating, or the state of being vibrated, or in vibratory motion; quick motion to and fro; oscillation, as of a pendulum or musical string. ; A limited reciprocating motion of a particle of an elastic body or medium in alternately opposite directions from its position of equilibrium, when that equilibrium has been disturbed, as when a stretched cord or other body produces musical notes, or particles of air transmit sounds to the ear. The path of the particle may be in a straight line, in a circular arc, or in any curve whatever.	a:m6r,57,15;ivy,44,10;1iek,37,17;20mz,28,5;1alp,26,9;gqu,22,2;lsa,6,5~1iek,37,17;m6r,57,15;ivy,44,10;1alp,26,9;lsa,6,5;20mz,28,5;gqu,22,2	v:m6r,38,4;2bik,27,4;15gl,18,3;cv7,11,3;2020,9,3~m6r,38,4;2bik,27,4;15gl,18,3;cv7,11,3;2020,9,3	V:1ltq,27,1;2031,27,3~2031,27,3;1ltq,27,1	n:1hk6,47,8;1uf2,47,5;gqu,38,6;ld4,6,3~1hk6,47,8;gqu,38,6;1uf2,47,5;ld4,6,3	N:15on,103,16;1ltt,79,18;274,78,5;24wl,67,9;on2,64,5;1ltq,59,9;1fdq,55,6;1el8,49,17;trg,45,10;1hk7,45,4;2032,31,9~1ltt,79,18;1el8,49,17;15on,103,16;trg,45,10;2032,31,9;1ltq,59,9;24wl,67,9;1fdq,55,6;274,78,5;on2,64,5;1hk7,45,4
